speechtext:
Speaking to the point of order, it seems to me, as the Prime Minister has said, that we are more or less agreed. It does not seem to me to serve the purpose of the Prime Minister to adopt the report in the
]Mr. Cahan.]
language in which it now appears, because, as worded, it will be a precedent with respect to the necessity of coming back to the house to obtain authority to deal with matters of this kind which have not originated in the current Auditor General's report. If the report of the committee is so amended as to provide for the consideration of items in the manner indicated, then we are all agreed upon it; but it cannot be accepted in the terms in which it now appears.

I had hoped to see in the
estimates provision for a public building at Biggar. The Postmaster General himself has admitted the need of such a building, and I thought from what the Minister of Public Works told me that he was not averse to having a public building erected in the town. Biggar has a population of three thousand, and the post office yields a yearly revenue of $11,000. It is a railway centre and growing 78594-123}
very fast. I think the minister knows the place very well. No suitable building is available for a post office. I do think the government should follow some well-defined policy in meeting the need for post offices in certain places. Gretna, although only one-fifth the size of Biggar, is being given a public building. Not only is Biggar a much larger town than Gretna, but its need for a public building is very urgent. I do not think it is fair to the people of Biggar to discriminate against them in this way. Seeing that the government does not follow any policy so far as population or need is concerned in allotting these grants, I should like to know what its policy really is. In looking over the estimates for Saskatchewan I see no grant is made to any but Liberal constituencies, and it does not seem fair that there should be this discrimination against Biggar when the need of proper post office facilities is so great.
